&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;h1&gt;📘 Topic: SOC 1 and SOC 2 Reports&lt;/h1&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Domain:&lt;/strong&gt; D1 – Security and Risk Management&lt;br&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Tags:&lt;/strong&gt; #cissp&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;hr&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;🧾 Definition&lt;span class=&#34;hx:absolute hx:-mt-20&#34; id=&#34;-definition&#34;&gt;&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;a href=&#34;#-definition&#34; class=&#34;subheading-anchor&#34; aria-label=&#34;Permalink for this section&#34;&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;SOC 1 and SOC 2 reports are independent assurance reports that help organizations evaluate controls and service provider trustworthiness. SOC 1 focuses on financial reporting controls, while SOC 2 focuses on security, availability, processing integrity, confidentiality, and privacy.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;hr&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;🔑 Key Points&lt;span class=&#34;hx:absolute hx:-mt-20&#34; id=&#34;-key-points&#34;&gt;&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;a href=&#34;#-key-points&#34; class=&#34;subheading-anchor&#34; aria-label=&#34;Permalink for this section&#34;&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;SOC 1 is commonly used for service organizations that affect financial reporting.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;SOC 2 is commonly used for cloud and technology providers and is based on Trust Services Criteria.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The report is prepared by an independent CPA firm and reflects management’s description of controls.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A SOC report supports vendor risk assessments and due diligence.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;hr&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;⚠️ CISSP Insight&lt;span class=&#34;hx:absolute hx:-mt-20&#34; id=&#34;-cissp-insight&#34;&gt;&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;a href=&#34;#-cissp-insight&#34; class=&#34;subheading-anchor&#34; aria-label=&#34;Permalink for this section&#34;&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;These reports are useful evidence during third-party risk management, but they are not a substitute for internal controls or a full compliance program.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;CISSP candidates should understand the purpose and audience of each report.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;hr&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;⚔️ Key Difference / Trap&lt;span class=&#34;hx:absolute hx:-mt-20&#34; id=&#34;-key-difference--trap&#34;&gt;&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;a href=&#34;#-key-difference--trap&#34; class=&#34;subheading-anchor&#34; aria-label=&#34;Permalink for this section&#34;&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;SOC 1 vs SOC 2&lt;/strong&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;SOC 1 = financial reporting controls&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;SOC 2 = security and trust services criteria&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;SOC 2 is not the same as ISO 27001 certification&lt;/strong&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;It is an attestation report, not a full management system certification&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;hr&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;🏗️ Example&lt;span class=&#34;hx:absolute hx:-mt-20&#34; id=&#34;-example&#34;&gt;&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;a href=&#34;#-example&#34; class=&#34;subheading-anchor&#34; aria-label=&#34;Permalink for this section&#34;&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;A SaaS provider shares a SOC 2 report with customers to demonstrate that its security controls are operating effectively over a period of time.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;hr&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;📚 References&lt;span class=&#34;hx:absolute hx:-mt-20&#34; id=&#34;-references&#34;&gt;&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;a href=&#34;#-references&#34; class=&#34;subheading-anchor&#34; aria-label=&#34;Permalink for this section&#34;&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;AICPA SOC 1 and SOC 2 guidance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;ISO/IEC 27001:2022&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;NIST Cybersecurity Framework&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;hr&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;🔁 Quick Recall&lt;span class=&#34;hx:absolute hx:-mt-20&#34; id=&#34;-quick-recall&#34;&gt;&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;a href=&#34;#-quick-recall&#34; class=&#34;subheading-anchor&#34; aria-label=&#34;Permalink for this section&#34;&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;SOC 1 = Finance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;SOC 2 = Security and Trust Services&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

      </description>
    </item>
    
    <item>
      <title>[09] Intellectual Property, Copyright, and Confidentiality</title>
      <link>http://localhost:1313/docs/04_playbooks/cissp/d1/09-patient/</link>
      <pubDate>Tue, 30 Jun 2026 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
      
      <guid>http://localhost:1313/docs/04_playbooks/cissp/d1/09-patient/</guid>
      <description>
        
        
        &lt;div style=&#34;margin-top: 1rem; margin-bottom: 2rem; font-size: 0.875rem; color: #6b7280; display: flex; align-items: center; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 10px;&#34;&gt;
  
    &lt;span style=&#34;display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 6px;&#34;&gt;
      By:
      
        
        
        
        
          
          
          
            
          
          
          &lt;a href=&#34;https://www.linkedin.com/in/prasannavbalaji&#34; target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noopener&#34; style=&#34;display: inline-flex; align-items: center; gap: 4px; font-weight: 600; color: #0a66c2; text-decoration: none; border-bottom: 1px solid transparent;&#34; onmouseover=&#34;this.style.borderBottom=&#39;1px solid #0a66c2&#39;&#34; onmouseout=&#34;this.style.borderBottom=&#39;1px solid transparent&#39;&#34;&gt;
            &lt;svg xmlns=&#34;http://www.w3.org/2000/svg&#34; width=&#34;14&#34; height=&#34;14&#34; viewBox=&#34;0 0 24 24&#34; fill=&#34;currentColor&#34;&gt;
                &lt;path d=&#34;M19 0h-14c-2.761 0-5 2.239-5 5v14c0 2.761 2.239 5 5 5h14c2.762 0 5-2.239 5-5v-14c0-2.761-2.238-5-5-5zm-11 19h-3v-11h3v11zm-1.5-12.268c-.966 0-1.75-.79-1.75-1.764s.784-1.764 1.75-1.764 1.75.79 1.75 1.764-.783 1.764-1.75 1.764zm13.5 12.268h-3v-5.604c0-3.368-4-3.113-4 0v5.604h-3v-11h3v1.765c1.396-2.586 7-2.777 7 2.476v6.759z&#34;/&gt;
